 "observations": [
  "The page number «210» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 95», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the left above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 92v, O 148v,» and «N 59r.», the second indented, the letters raised (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-209 (JP2 0238-0241): «Quinque gradus Geminorum» (L03), «Decem gradus Geminorum» (L15) and «Quindecim gradus Geminorum» (L23), the ascendant at 5°, 10° and 15° of Gemini, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold. The columns begin with the sign of the ascendant: «Gemini Sagittar. Horoscopus1)», «Cancer Capricorn. Horoscopus», «Leo Aquarius Horoscopus», «Virgo Pisces Horoscopus», «Libra Aries Horoscopus» and «Scorpius Taurus Horoscopus1)», where C has «Matale» (note 1); here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L05-L07), with «Gradus aequales», printed upwards, in L05-L06, and the units in L08. The numbers are counted from the beginning of Gemini. The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-209 (JP2 0238-0241), are a third, a half and two thirds of the last number of the field: 163° 59′ (L14) gives 54° 39.7′, 81° 59.5′ and 109° 19.3′, printed 54° 40′, 82° 0′ and 109° 19′ (L04); 167° 45′ (L22) gives 55° 55′, 83° 52.5′ and 111° 50′, printed 55° 55′, 83° 52′ and 111° 50′ (L16); 170° 7′ (L30) gives 56° 42.3′, 85° 3.5′ and 113° 24.7′, printed 56° 42′, 85° 3′ and 113° 24′ (L24), the 85 the editor's for the 75 of all three manuscripts (note f).",
  "The columns, as on pp. 208-209 (JP2 0240-0241): in Gemini and Cancer the three fields lie within 27′, 15′ and 23′ of the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Gemini for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′), except at 15° of Gemini in the second field (L19) and at 30° of Gemini in the third (L30; critical note); at the end of Scorpius they reach 163° 59′, 167° 45′ and 170° 7′, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Gemini is 214° 10′.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer in the trine of the first field (note a, L04: the 109° 19′ of O and N against C's «100. 9. 19»; two thirds of 163° 59′ are 109° 19.3′), at 30° of Cancer in the second (note b, L22: the 64 of O and N against C's 63; 63° 58′ and 64° 21′ in the other fields) and at 5° of Scorpius in the second (note d, L17: C's 147 against O's 141). At 20° of Virgo and 10° of Scorpius in the second field (notes c and e, L20, L18) the readings differ by 1′; neither is decided. The editor's 85 for the 75 of all three manuscripts in the quadrature of the third field (note f) is half of 170° 6′, as the other two numbers of its head.",
  "Without variants: in the second field 13° 0′ at 15° of Gemini (L19) lies 30′ and 55′ below the other fields (13° 30′, 13° 55′) and 32′ below the oblique ascension, 13° 32′, between the steps 4° 15′ and 5° 35′; 147° 5′ at 5° of Scorpius (L17) lies 52′ below the mean of the other fields (145° 34′, 150° 20′), between the steps 2° 33′ and 4° 43′, where the steps of the column run 3° 50′ to 4° 7′ after it. In the third field 74° 44′ at 10° of Leo (L26) lies below the other fields (74° 58′, 75° 21′), between the steps 4° 50′ and 6° 40′, and 142° 7′ at 25° of Libra (L29) between the steps 3° 4′ and 4° 33′.",
  "A speck above the o of «Horoscopus» over Libra (L07) and specks before the 55 and the 25 of Libra in L26-L27 and below the 1 of the 120 of Virgo in L29; not transcribed."
